@startuml
' Source of truth for: assets/diagrams/learning/data-plane/ngfw/steering-decision-tree.svg
' Re-render with: plantuml -tsvg steering-decision-tree.puml
title Steering Tag -> Pipeline Path\n(one ACL classification, six outcomes)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam rectangleRoundCorner 8
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

rectangle "ACL match\n-> steering tag" as ROOT #0f766e

rectangle "NONE\n-> ip4-lookup\n(default pass)" as R1 #f1f5f9
rectangle "NAT_PASS\n-> nat44 -> ip4-lookup\n(NAT then forward)" as R2 #f1f5f9
rectangle "SNORT_NAT\n-> snort -> nat44 -> ip4-lookup\n(inspect, NAT, forward)" as R3 #f1f5f9
rectangle "SNORT_NAT_IPSEC\n-> snort -> nat44 -> esp4-encrypt\n(inspect, NAT, VPN)" as R4 #f1f5f9
rectangle "NAT_IPSEC\n-> nat44 -> esp4-encrypt\n(NAT, VPN, no inspection)" as R5 #f1f5f9
rectangle "DROP\n-> error-drop\n(packet discarded)" as R6 #fef2f2

ROOT --> R1
ROOT --> R2
ROOT --> R3
ROOT --> R4
ROOT --> R5
ROOT --> R6

legend bottom
Inside ngfw-decision each tag maps to an action; a note in opaque2 carries the
"after Snort" part (NAT / IPsec / pass). The same six paths exist for IPv6 via the
mirror -ip6 nodes and nat66. Return traffic is matched by NAT/IPsec session state.
endlegend
@enduml
